   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 4.6,
     "end": 6.29,
     "lines": [
      "This is CardioLens."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 6.6,
     "end": 10.75,
     "lines": [
      "Routine clinical data goes in, and a 3D",
      "heart shows where coronary risk is likely"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.8,
     "end": 12.59,
     "lines": [
      "to be, artery by artery."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s01_problem",
   "title": "The problem",
   "chapter": 1,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "problem",
   "start": 465,
   "duration": 838,
   "lead": 0.6,
   "tail": 0.8,
   "voice": 26.54,
   "audio": "voice/s01_problem.wav",
   "cues": {
    "goal": 10.33,
    "table": 23.77
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.75,
     "end": 4.16,
     "lines": [
      "Cardiovascular disease remains a leading",
      "cause of death worldwide,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 4.21,
     "end": 8.34,
     "lines": [
      "and a narrowed coronary artery is usually",
      "confirmed by angiography,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 8.61,
     "end": 9.84,
     "lines": [
      "an invasive test."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.33,
     "end": 13.18,
     "lines": [
      "Track A asks a different question: can",
      "routine data,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.23,
     "end": 16.9,
     "lines": [
      "such as age, blood pressure, an ECG and a",
      "few lab values,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 16.95,
     "end": 20.759999999999998,
     "lines": [
      "predict coronary artery disease and the",
      "narrowing of each main artery,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 20.81,
     "end": 23.7,
     "lines": [
      "and show it on an interactive 3D model?"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 23.77,
     "end": 27.14,
     "lines": [
      "Here is every requirement, and where",
      "CardioLens meets it."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02a_data",
   "title": "Dataset and leakage rule",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "data",
   "start": 1348,
   "duration": 647,
   "lead": 0.4,
   "tail": 1.2,
   "voice": 19.96,
   "audio": "voice/s02a_data.wav",
   "cues": {
    "audit": 9.53,
    "leak": 13.27
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.55,
     "end": 3.8200000000000003,
     "lines": [
      "We used the extension of the Z-Alizadeh",
      "Sani dataset from UCI:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.87,
     "end": 7.22,
     "lines": [
      "303 patients, 55 features, and four",
      "targets: CAD,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 7.27,
     "end": 9.36,
     "lines": [
      "plus the LAD, LCX and RCA arteries."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 9.53,
     "end": 13.18,
     "lines": [
      "No values were missing, and a constant",
      "column was dropped."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.27,
     "end": 15.62,
     "lines": [
      "The label columns are never model inputs."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 15.67,
     "end": 19.08,
     "lines": [
      "That's asserted before every fit, and the",
      "API rejects them:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 19.31,
     "end": 20.36,
     "lines": [
      "requirement 1d."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02b_validation",
   "title": "Features and validation",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "validation",
   "start": 1995,
   "duration": 534,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 1.2,
   "voice": 16.3,
   "audio": "voice/s02b_validation.wav",
   "cues": {
    "holdout": 5.57,
    "cv": 8.77,
    "ci": 12.45
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.45,
     "end": 3.52,
     "lines": [
      "We add clinical features, such as a",
      "pretest probability,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.71,
     "end": 5.5200000000000005,
     "lines": [
      "kidney function and lipid ratios."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 5.57,
     "end": 8.719999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "Twenty percent of patients are held out",
      "until the very end."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 8.77,
     "end": 12.399999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "The rest go through five-by-five",
      "cross-validation with nested tuning,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 12.45,
     "end": 16.65,
     "lines": [
      "and confidence intervals come from a",
      "thousand bootstrap resamples."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02c_models",
   "title": "Models, strategies, calibration",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "models",
   "start": 2529,
   "duration": 640,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 1.2,
   "voice": 19.82,
   "audio": "voice/s02c_models.wav",
   "cues": {
    "strategy": 7.39,
    "calib": 13.95
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.45,
     "end": 3.3000000000000003,
     "lines": [
      "Nine model families were compared for",
      "every target,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.35,
     "end": 7.14,
     "lines": [
      "from logistic regression to boosting and",
      "stacked ensembles."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 7.39,
     "end": 12.02,
     "lines": [
      "For the arteries, independent models did",
      "as well as chained or hierarchical ones,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 12.07,
     "end": 13.68,
     "lines": [
      "so we kept the simplest."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.95,
     "end": 17.3,
     "lines": [
      "Every model is calibrated, so eighty",
      "percent means about eight in ten,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 17.35,
     "end": 20.12,
     "lines": [
      "with tuned thresholds and three risk",
      "tiers."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s02d_results",
   "title": "Results and explanations",
   "chapter": 2,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "results",
   "start": 3168,
   "duration": 560,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.8,
   "voice": 17.56,
   "audio": "voice/s02d_results.wav",
   "cues": {
    "shap": 11.13,
    "latency": 15.53
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.45,
     "end": 3.52,
     "lines": [
      "On the untouched hold-out set, the ROC-AUC",
      "is 0.895 for CAD,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.57,
     "end": 9.399999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "0.832 for LAD, 0.768 for LCX and 0.741 for",
      "RCA, with confidence intervals and every"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 9.45,
     "end": 11.08,
     "lines": [
      "metric from requirement 1e."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 11.13,
     "end": 13.62,
     "lines": [
      "Each estimate is explained with exact SHAP",
      "values,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.67,
     "end": 17.86,
     "lines": [
      "mapped back to the raw measurements, in",
      "about 150 milliseconds."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s03a_mapping",
   "title": "From probability to picture",
   "chapter": 3,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "mapping",
   "start": 3773,
   "duration": 687,
   "lead": 0.4,
   "tail": 1.2,
   "voice": 21.29,
   "audio": "voice/s03a_mapping.wav",
   "cues": {
    "scale": 10.725,
    "flag": 15.87
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.55,
     "end": 2.46,
     "lines": [
      "How does a probability become a picture?"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 2.67,
     "end": 6.36,
     "lines": [
      "One anatomy map holds every mesh name,",
      "colour and label,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 6.41,
     "end": 10.6,
     "lines": [
      "and a pure function turns each prediction",
      "into a render-ready scene."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.725,
     "end": 14.819999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "Colour shows probability, on one shared",
      "scale that is safe for colour-blind"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 14.87,
     "end": 18.439999999999998,
     "lines": [
      "viewers. Crossing a threshold adds an",
      "outline and a pulse,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 18.49,
     "end": 21.74,
     "lines": [
      "and every estimate carries a reliability",
      "badge."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s03b_rules",
   "title": "No over-claiming",
   "chapter": 3,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "rules",
   "start": 4460,
   "duration": 592,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.8,
   "voice": 18.64,
   "audio": "voice/s03b_rules.wav",
   "cues": {
    "overlays": 8.95,
    "whatif": 15.49
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.45,
     "end": 3.76,
     "lines": [
      "The data says whether an artery is",
      "narrowed, but not where."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.85,
     "end": 8.0,
     "lines": [
      "So whole arteries are coloured, and",
      "unlabelled branches stay neutral."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 8.95,
     "end": 12.299999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "Optional overlays show perfusion",
      "territories, and the body regions behind"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 12.35,
     "end": 15.32,
     "lines": [
      "each risk factor, never the disease",
      "itself."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 15.49,
     "end": 18.94,
     "lines": [
      "And what-if shows associations, not",
      "treatment effects."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s04a_source",
   "title": "The heart model",
   "chapter": 4,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "heart_source",
   "start": 5097,
   "duration": 580,
   "lead": 0.4,
   "tail": 1.2,
   "voice": 17.72,
   "audio": "voice/s04a_source.wav",
   "cues": {
    "sketchfab": 5.65
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.55,
     "end": 1.48,
     "lines": [
      "Building the heart."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 1.53,
     "end": 5.54,
     "lines": [
      "Our first version was a procedural heart,",
      "which is still kept as a fallback."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 5.65,
     "end": 9.78,
     "lines": [
      "For realism, we moved to the Realistic",
      "Human Heart by neshallads on Sketchfab,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 9.83,
     "end": 11.925,
     "lines": [
      "under CC BY 4.0."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 12.05,
     "end": 15.86,
     "lines": [
      "A headless Blender script aligns it,",
      "scales it to twelve centimetres,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 15.91,
     "end": 18.12,
     "lines": [
      "and splits it into parts."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s04b_build",
   "title": "Vessels and budgets",
   "chapter": 4,
   "kind": "card",
   "name": "heart_build",
   "start": 5677,
   "duration": 638,
   "lead": 0.3,
   "tail": 0.5,
   "voice": 20.48,
   "audio": "voice/s04b_build.wav",
   "cues": {
    "looks": 7.65,
    "lite": 13.27
   },
   "clips": [],
   "captions": [
    {
     "start": 0.45,
     "end": 4.68,
     "lines": [
      "Its coronaries were only painted on, so we",
      "traced them along the grooves,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 4.77,
     "end": 7.42,
     "lines": [
      "smoothed them, and swept them into real",
      "tubes."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 7.65,
     "end": 10.52,
     "lines": [
      "One file carries a realistic and a",
      "clinical look,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 10.57,
     "end": 13.219999999999999,
     "lines": [
      "plus invisible picking shapes and outline",
      "shells."
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 13.27,
     "end": 17.779999999999998,
     "lines": [
      "It's compressed to about 1.6 megabytes,",
      "with a lighter version for phones,"
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 17.83,
     "end": 20.78,
     "lines": [
      "and a validator checks every name and",
      "budget."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
